meta {
  name: Update student
  type: http
  seq: 17
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/students/{{studentId}}
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "student_code": "STU-2026-0001"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.student_code: eq STU-2026-0001
  res.body.status: eq active
}

docs {
  Only the school's own identifier is touched here, on purpose. status is
  editable through this route (active, alumni, withdrawn), but withdrawing the
  student would strand the enrolments folder 05 builds on top of this row, so
  this run leaves it alone.

  admission_number is unique per school, so it is the field that will bite you:
  a clash returns 409, and folder 09 has that case.

  Writable fields are decided per caller. Send a field your policy does not
  cover and the whole request is refused with a 403 naming it, rather than
  being applied in part - a partly-applied PATCH is impossible to reason about
  from the client side.
}
